    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d671">

                <pb facs="0818" n="532" xml:id="pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2912</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-30T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1916, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4793. Following from Wyvell:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>I will complete presentation of the 30 rejected cases and canceled permits
                        and of all pending cases I can submit next week. Decisions will in all cases
                        be rendered through the British Embassy at Washington and I will not be
                        informed of decisions. I would like to sail on <hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Paul
                        </hi> leaving September 9, as there will be nothing further to do here.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
